WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.600
According to the ICH GCP guidelines, there&nbsp;
three key roles in the clinical trial process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.360
The ethics committee representing&nbsp;
the regulatory authority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.920
the sponsor initiating and financing the project,&nbsp;
and the investigator conducts the research.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.040
Investigator&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:33.040
The ICH-GCP defines the investigator as "a person&nbsp;
responsible for the conduct of the clinical trial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.960
site. If a trial is conducted by a team of&nbsp;
individuals at a trial site, the investigator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.920
is the responsible leader of the team and&nbsp;
may be called the principal investigator."

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:50.320
Co-investigator is a term that pre-dates the&nbsp;
ICH-GCP. It has subsequently been replaced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:56.880
by the term sub-investigator. The ICH-GCP&nbsp;
defines sub-investigator as any individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.680
member of the clinical trial designated and&nbsp;
supervised by the investigator at a trial site&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.400
to perform critical trial-related procedures&nbsp;
or make important trial-related decisions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.840
These may include associates,&nbsp;
residents or research fellows.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.760
In a clinical trial, the responsibilities&nbsp;
of an investigator generally include:

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:21.680
1. Protecting the rights, safety and&nbsp;
welfare of subjects in the clinical study&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.720
2. Ensuring that informed consent is properly&nbsp;
obtained from clinical trial subjects&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.760
3. Conducting the clinical study and directly&nbsp;
overseeing the administration of the test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.640
products to the subject. In situations&nbsp;
where there is a team of researchers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.680
the investigator will act as the team leader
4. Ensuring that the clinical trial is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.520
conducted in accordance with the signed&nbsp;
agreement and the investigational plan&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.760
5. Controlling the products under&nbsp;
investigation including supervising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.240
medical-device use and disposal
6. Ensuring proper record-keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.560
and reporting requirements are met,&nbsp;
for example, mandatory safety reporting

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.080
Sponsor
In the conduct of a clinical trial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.760
a sponsor is an individual, institution, company&nbsp;
or organization that takes the responsibility to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.960
initiate, manage or finance the clinical trial,&nbsp;
but does not actually conduct the investigation.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.920
The specific requirements for a&nbsp;
clinical study sponsor can vary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.840
Generally, a sponsor is responsible for:

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:27.040
1. Selecting the investigators
2. Providing investigators with the necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.440
information to conduct the clinical trial
3. Ensuring proper monitoring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.720
of the clinical study
4. Ensuring all the necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.520
ethic reviews and approvals are obtained
5. Preparing and submitting clinical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.440
trial applications and amendments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.640
to the appropriate regulatory agencies
6. Ensuring that any reviewing ethics board&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.000
and regulatory agencies are promptly informed&nbsp;
of any significant new information, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.120
important findings that affect product safety
7. Ensuring compliance with labelling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.080
reporting and record-keeping requirements
8. Refraining from engaging in promotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:07.600
activities and other prohibited activities such as&nbsp;
commercializing an investigational medical device&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.800
9. Ensuring that the clinical study is conducted&nbsp;
in accordance with Good Clinical Practice

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.920
Sponsor-Investigator&nbsp;

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:26.080
A sponsor-investigator, on the other hand, takes&nbsp;
on the responsibility as a clinical study sponsor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:44.880
and also conducts or oversees the clinical&nbsp;
trial. Thus, a sponsor-investigator must comply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.200
with the applicable regulatory requirements that&nbsp;
pertain to both the sponsor and the investigator.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.800
Sponsor-investigators also generally&nbsp;
need to manage the following:

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:11.600
1. Securing funding for the clinical trial
2. Applying for the appropriate insurance&nbsp;

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:17.680
3. Generating the appropriate clinical trial&nbsp;
documentation (for example, informed consent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.320
protocols) and submissions (for example,&nbsp;
ethics and/or regulatory submissions)&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.760
4. Ensuring adequate resources are available&nbsp;
for the duration of the trial (for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.240
experienced staff, investigational and&nbsp;
control products, clinical and medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.560
supplies, an analytical laboratory)
5. Creating appropriate written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:42.000
procedures (for example, standard&nbsp;
operating procedures related to GCP)&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.560
6. Meeting all the applicable regulatory&nbsp;
requirements such as obtaining and maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.040
necessary approvals from the relevant&nbsp;
ethics review boards and regulatory agencies

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:57.120
Summary
In summary, the management of sponsor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:09.840
investigator relationship is of central importance&nbsp;
for planning and executing clinical trials.

